  "differences": [
    "Our periodic full-integration HEX8 analysis uses the full design grid; SCTOP uses coarse HEX20 analysis with sub-cell densities.",
    "Our Green/GJ/partial/ASG PCG runs on CUDA FP64; the paper uses direct solvers on a CPU. Published wall times are not same-hardware speedup benchmarks.",
    "Unit-cell edge is normalized from 0.1 to 1; effective moduli and normalized filter radii are invariant.",
    "Paper shear order [xy,yz,xz] is permuted from solver [yz,xz,xy] for tensor comparisons.",
    "Projection sweep is reconstructed on the basic 30^3 grid; the text does not explicitly identify its fixed resolution.",
    "The final accepted density is reanalyzed; the MATLAB log reports objective before the last OC update. Both are retained."
  ],
  "failure_policy": "Preserve failed runs and their last density; do not silently increase ersatz stiffness, switch solvers, or label budget termination convergence.",
